    Stack blocks: the invoke function named after its creator and typed.

    Issue: a block built on a method's frame (`isa = _NSConcreteStackBlock`, the
    invoke and descriptor addresses stored after it) left its invoke function a
    `sub_` with an untyped first argument, so a captured variable read as an
    offset off an unknown pointer.

    Fix: `analyzers/objc/kuna_objcblocks.rs (stack_blocks)` scans each arm64
    function for the isa's GOT load (`adrp; ldr`, or the linker's `ldr literal`),
    its store to `sp`, and the `adr`/`adrp; add` addresses stored 16 and 24
    bytes after it (`str`/`stp`); the invoke is named `<creator>_block_invoke`,
    typed from the descriptor's signature, with `Block_layout_<invoke>` carrying
    one word per captured value up to the descriptor's size.

    Pass 1 (`objc off`): `sub_100000814`. Pass 2 (`objc on`):
    `long -[Runner maker:]_block_invoke(Block_layout_100000814 *block,long arg1)
    { return block->capture_0 * arg1; }`.
-->
